cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MyoSim in academic work, cite this software release and the declared task, replay, and provenance bundle."
title: "MyoSim: Reproducible Motor-Intent to Simulated-Action Research Demonstrator"
abstract: >-
  A local-first, software-only, non-clinical research platform for deterministic
  replay of motor-intent records through confidence-aware decision logic, bounded
  control, virtual prosthetic simulation, task metrics and provenance reporting.
  Version 0.1.6 adds a recorded-data downstream integration (NinaPro DB3/DB7-derived
  decoder predictions replayed through the control stack) and an opt-in Hardware Twin
  actuator model whose parameters are assumptions, with a frozen sensitivity matrix.
  This release does not establish clinical validation, hardware safety, decoder
  efficacy, or biomechanical equivalence.
type: software
